en\",\"tgt_lang\":\"zh-CN\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-01T12:51:58Z\"}\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\.i18n\\zh-CN.tm.jsonl:1250: {\"cache_key\":\"f25bc202081adc9aa4d305452fe50f1a9c63b9077c112ebdc0d9166737b3675a\",\"segment_id\":\"index.md:99260acc29f71e4b\",\"source_path\":\"index.md\",\"text_hash\":\"99260acc29f71e4baeb36805a1fdbd2c17254b57c8e5a9cba29ee56518832397\",\"text\":\" �� Route provider accounts/peers to isolated agents (workspace + per-agent sessions)\",\"translated\":\" �� �� �ṩ�� �˻�/�Եȷ�·�ɵ������ �����壨������ + ÿ�� ������ �� �Ự��\",\"provider\":\"pi\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5\",\"src_lang\":\"en\",\"tgt_lang\":\"zh-CN\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-01T13:01:46Z\"}\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\cron-jobs.md:105: - optional **agent binding** (`agentId`): run the job under a specific agent; if\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\cron-jobs.md:171: - `systemEvent`: main-session only, routed through the heartbeat prompt.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\cron-jobs.md:250: ��last route�� (the last place the agent replied).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\cron-jobs.md:318: - Optional fields: `agentId`, `description`, `enabled`, `deleteAfterRun` (defaults to true for `at`),\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\cron-jobs.md:337: - Use `agentId: null` in the patch to clear an agent binding.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\cron-jobs.md:556: Agent selection (multi-agent setups):\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\cron-jobs.md:625: - If you see `telegram:...` prefixes in logs or stored ��last route�� targets, that��s normal;\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\gmail-pubsub.md:63: uses the last delivery route (falls back to WhatsApp).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\gmail-pubsub.md:75:       model: \"openrouter/meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:221:     senderId?: string,\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:271:   from: string,           // Sender identifier (phone number, user ID, etc.)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:283:     senderId?: string,\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:284:     senderName?: string,\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:285:     senderUsername?: string,\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:286:     senderE164?: string,\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:548: - **Session Key**: agent:main:main\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:618: 1. Captures event details (command action, timestamp, session key, sender ID, source)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:625: {\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-16T14:30:00.000Z\",\"action\":\"new\",\"sessionKey\":\"agent:main:main\",\"senderId\":\"+1234567890\",\"source\":\"telegram\"}\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:626: {\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-16T15:45:22.000Z\",\"action\":\"stop\",\"sessionKey\":\"agent:main:main\",\"senderId\":\"user@example.com\",\"source\":\"whatsapp\"}\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:21:     // Optional: restrict explicit `agentId` routing to this allowlist.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:23:     // Set [] to deny all explicit `agentId` routing.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:24:     allowedAgentIds: [\"hooks\", \"main\"],\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:68:   \"agentId\": \"hooks\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:82: - `agentId` optional (string): Route this hook to a specific agent. Unknown IDs fall back to the default agent. When set, the hook runs using the resolved agent's workspace and configuration.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:94: - Runs an **isolated** agent turn (own session key)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:98: ## Session key policy (breaking change)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:145: - Use `match.source` to keep a generic ingest endpoint (payload-driven routing).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:147: - Set `deliver: true` + `channel`/`to` on mappings to route replies to a chat surface\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:149: - `agentId` routes the hook to a specific agent; unknown IDs fall back to the default agent.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:150: - `hooks.allowedAgentIds` restricts explicit `agentId` routing. Omit it (or include `*`) to allow any agent. Set `[]` to deny explicit `agentId` routing.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:209: - If you use multi-agent routing, set `hooks.allowedAgentIds` to limit explicit `agentId` selection.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:21: - Pairing/allowlist works the same way as other channels (`/channels/pairing` etc) with `channels.bluebubbles.allowFrom` + pairing codes.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:153: - Unknown senders receive a pairing code; messages are ignored until approved (codes expire after 1 hour).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:162: - `channels.bluebubbles.groupAllowFrom` controls who can trigger in groups when `allowlist` is set.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:170: - Control commands from authorized senders bypass mention gating.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:179:       groupAllowFrom: [\"+15555550123\"],\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:192: - Uses `allowFrom` and `groupAllowFrom` to determine command authorization.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:193: - Authorized senders can run control commands even without mentioning in groups.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:299: - `channels.bluebubbles.allowFrom`: DM allowlist (handles, emails, E.164 numbers, `chat_id:*`, `chat_guid:*`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:301: - `channels.bluebubbles.groupAllowFrom`: Group sender allowlist.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:321: Prefer `chat_guid` for stable routing:\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:5:   - Debugging multi-agent replies in WhatsApp\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:161:    - Each agent has its own session key and isolated context\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:164:    - Normal routing applies (first matching binding)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:172: - **Session keys** (`agent:alfred:whatsapp:group:120363...` vs `agent:baerbel:whatsapp:group:120363...`)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:284: ### Routing\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:286: Broadcast groups work alongside existing routing:\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:293:       \"agentId\": \"alfred\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:302: - `GROUP_A`: Only alfred responds (normal routing)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:440: - [Multi-Agent Configuration](/tools/multi-agent-sandbox-tools)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:441: - [Routing Configuration](/channels/channel-routing)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:2: summary: \"Routing rules per channel (WhatsApp, Telegram, Discord, Slack) and shared context\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:4:   - Changing channel routing or inbox behavior\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:5: title: \"Channel Routing\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:8: # Channels & routing\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:10: OpenClaw routes replies **back to the channel where a message came from**. The\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:11: model does not choose a channel; routing is deterministic and controlled by the\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:18: - **AgentId**: an isolated workspace + session store (��brain��).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:21: ## Session key shapes (examples)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:25: - `agent:<agentId>:<mainKey>` (default: `agent:main:main`)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:29: - Groups: `agent:<agentId>:<channel>:group:<id>`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:30: - Channels/rooms: `agent:<agentId>:<channel>:channel:<id>`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:42: ## Routing rules (how an agent is chosen)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:44: Routing picks **one agent** for each inbound message:\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:90:     { match: { channel: \"slack\", teamId: \"T123\" }, agentId: \"support\" },\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:91:     { match: { channel: \"telegram\", peer: { kind: \"group\", id: \"-100123\" } }, agentId: \"support\" },\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:100: - `~/.openclaw/agents/<agentId>/sessions/sessions.json`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:103: You can override the store path via `session.store` and `{agentId}` templating.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\channel-routing.md:115: - `ReplyToId`, `ReplyToBody`, and `ReplyToSender` when available."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1287,"aggregated":"C:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:99:       \"source\": \"/openrouter\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:100:       \"destination\": \"/providers/openrouter\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:515:       \"source\": \"/multi-agent\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:516:       \"destination\": \"/concepts/multi-agent\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:555:       \"source\": \"/provider-routing\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:556:       \"destination\": \"/channels/channel-routing\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:559:       \"source\": \"/concepts/provider-routing\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:560:       \"destination\": \"/channels/channel-routing\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:922:                   \"channels/channel-routing\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:960:                 \"group\": \"Multi-agent\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:961:                 \"pages\": [\"concepts/multi-agent\", \"concepts/presence\"]\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:1009:                   \"tools/multi-agent-sandbox-tools\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:1074:                   \"providers/openrouter\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:1456:                   \"zh-CN/channels/channel-routing\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:1495:                 \"pages\": [\"zh-CN/concepts/multi-agent\", \"zh-CN/concepts/presence\"]\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:1542:                   \"zh-CN/tools/multi-agent-sandbox-tools\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\docs.json:1607:                   \"zh-CN/providers/openrouter\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\index.md:54: - **Agent-native**: built for coding agents with tool use, sessions, memory, and multi-agent routing\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\index.md:71: The Gateway is the single source of truth for sessions, routing, and channel connections.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\index.md:82:   <Card title=\"Multi-agent routing\" icon=\"route\">\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\index.md:83:     Isolated sessions per agent, workspace, or sender.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\index.md:134: - If you **do nothing**, OpenClaw uses the bundled Pi binary in RPC mode with per-sender sessions.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\index.md:135: - If you want to lock it down, start with `channels.whatsapp.allowFrom` and (for groups) mention rules.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\n