169a2c1043c188191a5959c21f689f92c","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"Get-ChildItem -Path \"C:\\Users\\吗喽\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\" -Recurse -File | Select-String -Pattern \"dmPolicy|pairing|allowFrom|approve|pair code\" | Select-Object -First 80 | ForEach-Object { \"$($_.Path):$($_.LineNumber): $($_.Line)\" }","workdir":"C:\\Users\\吗喽\\.openclaw\\workspace"},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"Get-ChildItem -Path \\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\吗喽\\\\AppData\\\\Roaming\\\\npm\\\\node_modules\\\\openclaw\\\\docs\\\\channels\\\" -Recurse -File | Select-String -Pattern \\\"dmPolicy|pairing|allowFrom|approve|pair code\\\" | Select-Object -First 80 | ForEach-Object { \\\"$($_.Path):$($_.LineNumber): $($_.Line)\\\" }\",\"workdir\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\吗喽\\\\.openclaw\\\\workspace\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.3-codex","usage":{"input":1850,"output":216,"cacheRead":91008,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":93074,"cost":{"input":0.0032375,"output":0.0030239999999999998,"cacheRead":0.0159264,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0221879}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772273919125}}
{"type":"message","id":"d46d3f16","parentId":"a4c5d39b","timestamp":"2026-02-28T10:18:47.303Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_MjsDk6J3QMjcORPMXpkdcO1P|fc_022820e6e342404f0169a2c1043c188191a5959c21f689f92c","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"C:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:2: summary: \"iMessage via BlueBubbles macOS server (REST send/receive, typing, reactions, pairing, advanced actions).\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:5:   - Troubleshooting webhook pairing\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:21: - Pairing/allowlist works the same way as other channels (`/channels/pairing` etc) with `channels.bluebubbles.allowFrom` + pairing codes.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:45: 5. Start the gateway; it will register the webhook handler and start pairing.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:117: - The first run may trigger macOS **Automation** prompts (`osascript` �� Messages). Approve them in the same user session that runs the LaunchAgent.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:139: - **DM policy**: pairing, allowlist, open, or disabled\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:152: - Default: `channels.bluebubbles.dmPolicy = \"pairing\"`.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:153: - Unknown senders receive a pairing code; messages are ignored until approved (codes expire after 1 hour).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:154: - Approve via:\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:155:   - `openclaw pairing list bluebubbles`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:156:   - `openclaw pairing approve bluebubbles <CODE>`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:157: - Pairing is the default token exchange. Details: [Pairing](/channels/pairing)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:162: - `channels.bluebubbles.groupAllowFrom` controls who can trigger in groups when `allowlist` is set.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:179:       groupAllowFrom: [\"+15555550123\"],\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:192: - Uses `allowFrom` and `groupAllowFrom` to determine command authorization.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:298: - `channels.bluebubbles.dmPolicy`: `pairing | allowlist | open | disabled` (default: `pairing`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:299: - `channels.bluebubbles.allowFrom`: DM allowlist (handles, emails, E.164 numbers, `chat_id:*`, `chat_guid:*`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:301: - `channels.bluebubbles.groupAllowFrom`: Group sender allowlist.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:339: - Pairing codes expire after one hour; use `openclaw pairing list bluebubbles` and `openclaw pairing approve bluebubbles <code>`.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:13:   <Card title=\"Pairing\" icon=\"link\" href=\"/channels/pairing\">\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:14:     Discord DMs default to pairing mode.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:89:     For pairing to work, Discord needs to allow your bot to DM you. Right-click your **server icon** �� **Privacy Settings** �� toggle on **Direct Messages**.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:91:     This lets server members (including bots) send you DMs. Keep this enabled if you want to use Discord DMs with OpenClaw. If you only plan to use guild channels, you can disable DMs after pairing.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:141:   <Step title=\"Approve first DM pairing\">\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:142:     Wait until the gateway is running, then DM your bot in Discord. It will respond with a pairing code.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:146:         Send the pairing code to your agent on your existing channel:\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:148:         > \"Approve this Discord pairing code: `<CODE>`\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:153: openclaw pairing list discord\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:154: openclaw pairing approve discord <CODE>\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:160:     Pairing codes expire after 1 hour.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:328:             label: \"Approve\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:370:     `channels.discord.dmPolicy` controls DM access (legacy: `channels.discord.dm.policy`):\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:372:     - `pairing` (default)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:374:     - `open` (requires `channels.discord.allowFrom` to include `\"*\"`; legacy: `channels.discord.dm.allowFrom`)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:377:     If DM policy is not open, unknown users are blocked (or prompted for pairing in `pairing` mode).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:381:     - `channels.discord.accounts.default.allowFrom` applies only to the `default` account.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:382:     - Named accounts inherit `channels.discord.allowFrom` when their own `allowFrom` is unset.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:383:     - Named accounts do not inherit `channels.discord.accounts.default.allowFrom`.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:844:     - `channels.discord.execApprovals.approvers`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:848:     When `target` is `channel` or `both`, the approval prompt is visible in the channel. Only configured approvers can use the buttons; other users receive an ephemeral denial. Approval prompts include the command text, so only enable channel delivery in trusted channels. If the channel ID cannot be derived from the session key, OpenClaw falls back to DM delivery.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:850:     If approvals fail with unknown approval IDs, verify approver list and feature enablement.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:1010:   <Accordion title=\"DM and pairing issues\">\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:1013:     - DM policy disabled: `channels.discord.dmPolicy=\"disabled\"` (legacy: `channels.discord.dm.policy`)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:1014:     - awaiting pairing approval in `pairing` mode\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:1066: - [Pairing](/channels/pairing)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:160: 3. Wait for admin approval (enterprise apps usually auto-approve)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:183:       dmPolicy: \"pairing\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:239: ### 3. Approve pairing\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:241: By default, the bot replies with a pairing code. Approve it:\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:244: openclaw pairing approve feishu <CODE>\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:264: - **Default**: `dmPolicy: \"pairing\"` (unknown users get a pairing code)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:265: - **Approve pairing**:\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:268:   openclaw pairing list feishu\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:269:   openclaw pairing approve feishu <CODE>\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:272: - **Allowlist mode**: set `channels.feishu.allowFrom` with allowed Open IDs\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:279: - `\"allowlist\"` = only allow `groupAllowFrom`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:325:       groupAllowFrom: [\"ou_xxx\", \"ou_yyy\"],\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:359: Check pairing requests for user Open IDs:\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:362: openclaw pairing list feishu\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:400: 1. Ensure the app is published and approved\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:544: | `channels.feishu.dmPolicy`                        | DM policy                       | `pairing`        |\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:545: | `channels.feishu.allowFrom`                       | DM allowlist (open_id list)     | -                |\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:547: | `channels.feishu.groupAllowFrom`                  | Group allowlist                 | -                |\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:557: ## dmPolicy reference\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:561: | `\"pairing\"`   | **Default.** Unknown users get a pairing code; must be approved |\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:562: | `\"allowlist\"` | Only users in `allowFrom` can chat                              |\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:563: | `\"open\"`      | Allow all users (requires `\"*\"` in allowFrom)                   |\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\googlechat.md:148: 4. DM access is pairing by default. Unknown senders receive a pairing code; approve with:\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\googlechat.md:149:    - `openclaw pairing approve googlechat <code>`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\googlechat.md:175:         policy: \"pairing\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\googlechat.md:176:         allowFrom: [\"users/1234567890\"],\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\grammy.md:23: - **Config knobs:** `channels.telegram.botToken`, `channels.telegram.dmPolicy`, `channels.telegram.groups` (allowlist + mention defaults), `channels.telegram.allowFrom`, `channels.telegram.groupAllowFrom`, `channels.telegram.groupPolicy`, `channels.telegram.mediaMaxMb`, `channels.telegram.linkPreview`, `channels.telegram.proxy`, `channels.telegram.webhookSecret`, `channels.telegram.webhookUrl`, `channels.telegram.webhookHost`.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\group-messages.md:17: - Group policy: `channels.whatsapp.groupPolicy` controls whether group messages are accepted (`open|disabled|allowlist`). `allowlist` uses `channels.whatsapp.groupAllowFrom` (fallback: explicit `channels.whatsapp.allowFrom`). Default is `allowlist` (blocked until you add senders).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\group-messages.md:63: Only the owner number (from `channels.whatsapp.allowFrom`, or the bot��s own E.164 when unset) can change this. Send `/status` as a standalone message in the group to see the current activation mode.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\groups.md:26: > - **DM access** is controlled by `*.allowFrom`.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\groups.md:27: > - **Group access** is controlled by `*.groupPolicy` + allowlists (`*.groups`, `*.groupAllowFrom`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\groups.md:48: | Only you can trigger in groups               | `groupPolicy: \"allowlist\"`, `groupAllowFrom: [\"+1555...\"]` |\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\groups.md:137:       groupAllowFrom: [\"+15551234567\"],\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\groups.md:141:       groupAllowFrom: [\"123456789\"], // numeric Telegram user id (wizard can resolve @username)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\groups.md:145:       groupAllowFrom: [\"+15551234567\"],"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":427,"aggregated":"C:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:2: summary: \"iMessage via BlueBubbles macOS server (REST send/receive, typing, reactions, pairing, advanced actions).\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:5:   - Troubleshooting webhook pairing\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:21: - Pairing/allowlist works the same way as other channels (`/channels/pairing` etc) with `channels.bluebubbles.allowFrom` + pairing codes.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:45: 5. Start the gateway; it will register the webhook handler and start pairing.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:117: - The first run may trigger macOS **Automation** prompts (`osascript` �� Messages). Approve them in the same user session that runs the LaunchAgent.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:139: - **DM policy**: pairing, allowlist, open, or disabled\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:152: - Default: `channels.bluebubbles.dmPolicy = \"pairing\"`.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:153: - Unknown senders receive a pairing code; messages are ignored until approved (codes expire after 1 hour).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:154: - Approve via:\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:155:   - `openclaw pairing list bluebubbles`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:156:   - `openclaw pairing approve bluebubbles <CODE>`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:157: - Pairing is the default token exchange. Details: [Pairing](/channels/pairing)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:162: - `channels.bluebubbles.groupAllowFrom` controls who can trigger in groups when `allowlist` is set.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:179:       groupAllowFrom: [\"+15555550123\"],\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:192: - Uses `allowFrom` and `groupAllowFrom` to determine command authorization.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:298: - `channels.bluebubbles.dmPolicy`: `pairing | allowlist | open | disabled` (default: `pairing`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:299: - `channels.bluebubbles.allowFrom`: DM allowlist (handles, emails, E.164 numbers, `chat_id:*`, `chat_guid:*`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:301: - `channels.bluebubbles.groupAllowFrom`: Group sender allowlist.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:339: - Pairing codes expire after one hour; use `openclaw pairing list bluebubbles` and `openclaw pairing approve bluebubbles <code>`.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:13:   <Card title=\"Pairing\" icon=\"link\" href=\"/channels/pairing\">\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:14:     Discord DMs default to pairing mode.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:89:     For pairing to work, Discord needs to allow your bot to DM you. Right-click your **server icon** �� **Privacy Settings** �� toggle on **Direct Messages**.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:91:     This lets server members (including bots) send you DMs. Keep this enabled if you want to use Discord DMs with OpenClaw. If you only plan to use guild channels, you can disable DMs after pairing.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:141:   <Step title=\"Approve first DM pairing\">\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:142:     Wait until the gateway is running, then DM your bot in Discord. It will respond with a pairing code.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:146:         Send the pairing code to your agent on your existing channel:\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:148:         > \"Approve this Discord pairing code: `<CODE>`\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:153: openclaw pairing list discord\